I estimated the plate at about 24 cm across, which makes it a dinner-plate size. The tuna salad mound is roughly 8 to 9 cm wide and 9 cm tall in the photo, and I judged it to be about 2.5 cm high. That gives a volume of about 130 cm³ and a weight of about 120 g.

The salad looks like tuna mixed with celery, red onion and a creamy dressing. I split it into separate items on that basis. The shredded carrot on the side plate is only partly in frame, so I did not count it. The few carrot shreds on top of the salad are included as a small item.

